itter  followers I have or tell me how many  YouTube subscribers I have and make sure  that you respond to this application  with that answer in the first line and  so does a couple things why not make  sure that they actually read the entire  post because a lot of people will apply  to a job without ever having reading the  post just because it says mechanic or  technician or programmer or whatever it  is they just apply and it takes them  five seconds to do it and it takes your  time to read their resume and read their  cover letter and so I don't want people  chewing up my time if they haven't even  taken the time to read the job posting  to it's a pretty simple easy thing for  them to do but you'd be surprised at how  many people I get who write in the say  I'd be happy to tell you  how many Facebook fans you have what's  the link your facebook page it is not  that hard to find me right if you can't  go to facebook and look for Evan  Carmichael then you're probably not  going to be a good fit in an  entrepreneurial kind of environment  right and so that helps weed out a ton  of people i we doubt I would say as many  as seventy percent of the people never  answer that question and that's amazing  because that just cut down my work by  seventy percent and having to read  applications next I don't do interviews  I think they're huge waste of time and  again that they don't test for the  skills that you need them to do in your  actual job the next thing I do is I do a  paint trial for everybody who wrote to  me with the answer then I will give them  a paid trial and I'll give them a task  that will be similar to what they have  to do in real life working for me so if  it's repairing farm equipment it'll be a  task that I think will take up to I  would say two hours to do and I'll give  them up to five hours to do it and so 1  i'm testing their skills testing their  abilities and 2 i'm also testing to see  if they're milking me for the full five  hours or not it'll b